{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-matthew-028",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 28,
  "title": "Matthew 28",
  "display_title": "Matthew 28",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "matthew",
  "book": "Matthew",
  "bookName": "Matthew",
  "bookOrder": 40,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 28,
  "sortOrder": 40028,
  "verseCount": 20,
  "aliases": [
    "Matt",
    "Mt"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "In the end of the sabbath, as it began to dawn toward the first day of the week, came Mary Magdalene and the other Mary to see the sepulchre.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "And, behold, there was a great earthquake: for the angel of the Lord descended from heaven, and came and rolled back the stone from the door, and sat upon it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "His countenance was like lightning, and his raiment white as snow:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "And for fear of him the keepers did shake, and became as dead men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "And the angel answered and said unto the women, Fear not ye: for I know that ye seek Jesus, which was crucified.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "He is not here: for he is risen, as he said. Come, see the place where the Lord lay.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "And go quickly, and tell his disciples that he is risen from the dead; and, behold, he goeth before you into Galilee; there shall ye see him: lo, I have told you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "And they departed quickly from the sepulchre with fear and great joy; and did run to bring his disciples word.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "And as they went to tell his disciples, behold, Jesus met them, saying, All hail. And they came and held him by the feet, and worshipped him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Then said Jesus unto them, Be not afraid: go tell my brethren that they go into Galilee, and there shall they see me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Now when they were going, behold, some of the watch came into the city, and shewed unto the chief priests all the things that were done.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "And when they were assembled with the elders, and had taken counsel, they gave large money unto the soldiers,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Saying, Say ye, His disciples came by night, and stole him away while we slept.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "And if this come to the governor’s ears, we will persuade him, and secure you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "So they took the money, and did as they were taught: and this saying is commonly reported among the Jews until this day.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Then the eleven disciples went away into Galilee, into a mountain where Jesus had appointed them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And when they saw him, they worshipped him: but some doubted.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "And Jesus came and spake unto them, saying, All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Go ye therefore, and teach all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Ghost:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:28:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Teaching them to observe all things whatsoever I have commanded you: and, lo, I am with you alway, even unto the end of the world. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 28:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:28:20"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
